<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Session-exit daily metric — one reading a day, with no Claude session as its parent.

  WHY THIS EXISTS. The store at `~/.claude/state/session-exit/` recorded a jump from 2
  unexplained session deaths on 2026-10-27 to 37 on 2026-10-28, and nobody saw it for four
  days, because seeing it meant remembering to run a shell pipeline over 200+ files. A
  metric that only exists while someone is looking is not a metric; this agent is what
  makes the next step change visible on the day it happens.

  WHY LAUNCHD, and not a detached loop: a detached loop can die silently and take the
  measurement with it, which is the failure mode being measured. `StartCalendarInterval`
  runs a fresh process, so there is no loop to die. Same shape as
  `com.bborbe.fleet-keeper.plist` and `com.bborbe.flow-push-victoriametrics.plist`.

  WHY 23:50 AND `--days 1`: the unit is a calendar day, and the log is meant to carry
  exactly one line per day. A window wider than one day re-prints earlier days on every
  run, which makes a stopped agent and a quiet one indistinguishable — the previous 13
  days still sit in the log. One line per run is what makes "no line for yesterday" mean
  "the agent did not run" and nothing else. `daily --days N` zero-fills, so a day with no
  deaths prints `ends=0` rather than vanishing.

  ⚠️ **The day boundary is UTC, not local.** Records are stamped `now_utc()` and bucketed
  on the timestamp's first ten characters, so at 23:50 Berlin (21:50 UTC in summer) the
  "today" row is provisional — it is complete only once the UTC day rolls over. The next
  evening's line is the final one. Bucketing by local date would need the store's stamps
  to change too; stating it here is the honest option until they do.

  `RunAtLoad` fires one on install, so the metric has a baseline the moment it is wired
  rather than the next evening.

  ⚠️ **Every path here is absolute, and that is a launchd requirement, not an oversight.**
  launchd does not expand `~`, does not inherit the shell's `PATH`, and does not resolve a
  relative interpreter — so a plist carrying `~/…` is a plist that silently never runs.
  The same is true of `launchd/com.bborbe.fleet-keeper.plist` beside this file. This is the
  one place in the repo where a machine-local path is the correct value.

  The script path is the marketplace clone, not a version-pinned cache dir: a cache path
  would pin the agent to one release and silently run stale code after every upgrade.

  Install:
    cp launchd/com.bborbe.session-exit-daily.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.bborbe.session-exit-daily.plist

  Reload after an upgrade:
    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.bborbe.session-exit-daily
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.bborbe.session-exit-daily</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/Users/bborbe/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/claude-supervisor/scripts/session-exit-record.py</string>
        <string>daily</string>
        <string>--line</string>
        <string>--days</string>
        <string>1</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>23</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>50</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/bborbe/Library/Logs/session-exit-daily.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/bborbe/Library/Logs/session-exit-daily.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
